<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/content.css</code></li>
    <li>Behaviour <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/wwwroot/dnf.js</code> (copy: <code>data-copy-text</code>, <code>data-copy-target</code>)</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A code block shows read-only code, a token or a URL in a monospaced block that wraps long lines. Add a copy button
    in its corner with <code>dnf-code-block__copy</code>; <code>dnf.js</code> copies on click and confirms with a toast.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <pre class="dnf-code-block">dnf_1a2b3c4d_9f8e7d6c5b4a39281706f5e4d3c2b1a0<dnf-button size="Sm" icon="copy" class="dnf-code-block__copy" data-copy-text="dnf_1a2b3c4d_9f8e7d6c5b4a39281706f5e4d3c2b1a0">Copy</dnf-button></pre>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="plain" title="Without a copy button" description="Just the block: code background and colour, monospace text, wrapped lines." layout="block">
    <pre class="dnf-code-block">curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" https://www.example.com/api/entries/articles</pre>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="copy-target" title="Copy a part" description="data-copy-target copies the text of another element - here the code element inside the block, so the button's own label is left out." layout="block">
    <pre class="dnf-code-block"><code id="code-block-env">DATABASE_CONNECTION_STRING=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Username=postgres
SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com</code><dnf-button size="Sm" icon="copy" class="dnf-code-block__copy" data-copy-target="#code-block-env">Copy</dnf-button></pre>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="inline" title="Inline" description="dnf-code-block--inline is a small borderless block on a code element that wraps like text - an API path under a heading." layout="block">
    <code class="dnf-code-block dnf-code-block--inline">GET /api/entries/articles?sort=-createdAt&amp;limit=20</code>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="scroll" title="Scrolling" description="dnf-code-block--scroll caps the block at 18rem and scrolls; it breaks lines only where it must." layout="block">
    <pre class="dnf-code-block dnf-code-block--scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Response">{
  "data": [
    { "id": 1, "title": "Why we built a CMS", "status": "published", "updatedAt": "2026-10-03T14:05:00Z" },
