<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="Utilities beat the block's styles - smaller text, a lower maximum height." layout="block">
    <pre class="dnf-code-block dnf-code-block--scroll text-xs max-h-24" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Query">SELECT id, title, status
FROM entries
WHERE content_type = 'articles'
ORDER BY updated_at DESC
LIMIT 20;</pre>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="The code block has no component tokens (its colours are the global code tokens); restyle it in a scope with your own (unlayered) CSS - here on the muted surface." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-code">
        <pre class="dnf-code-block">dotnet run --project src/DotNetForge.Web</pre>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-code .dnf-code-block {
    background: var(--dnf-surface-muted);
    color: var(--dnf-foreground);
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-code-block</code></td><td>block</td><td><code>--dnf-code-background</code> and <code>--dnf-code-foreground</code>, monospace <code>text-sm</code>, line height 1.6, wraps (<code>pre-wrap</code>, breaks anywhere), scrolls sideways if it must</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-code-block__copy</code></td><td>element</td><td>a button in the top-end corner; the block keeps 6rem free for it</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-code-block--inline</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>a small borderless block that wraps like normal text</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-code-block--scroll</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>at most 18rem high, scrolls; breaks lines only where it must</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>invalid</td><td><code>[data-invalid="true"]</code></td><td>the text in <code>--dnf-danger</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>The code block has no tag helper: the classes above are its API. Copying is a <code>dnf.js</code> behaviour of any
    button (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/behaviours">Behaviours</a>):</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>On</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data-copy-text="value"</code></td><td>a button</td><td>copies the value (trimmed) and shows "Copied to clipboard." or an error toast</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-copy-target="#id"</code></td><td>a button</td><td>copies the target's value if it is an input, else its text</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The copy button needs a name - its text, or an <code>aria-label</code> when it shows only the <code>copy</code> icon.</li>
    <li>Success and failure of a copy are announced by the toast.</li>
    <li>A block that scrolls (<code>--scroll</code>) needs <code>tabindex="0"</code>, <code>role="region"</code> and an <code>aria-label</code>, so keyboard users can focus and scroll it.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use <code>data-copy-text</code>, or a <code>data-copy-target</code> on an inner element, for a block that holds its copy button - copying the whole block would include the button's label.</li>
    <li>Do show a secret once, in a code block with a copy button, and say that it won't be shown again.</li>
    <li>Don't put editable code here - use a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/textarea">textarea</a> with <code>dnf-textarea--code</code>.</li>
</ul>
